  "body": "Related to https://github.com/WICG/async-cookies-api/issues/37\r\n\r\nShould this API (working in the world of JavaScript) be allowed to create `httpOnly` cookies?\r\n\r\nThis is currently not possible from JavaScript within the web page:\r\n\r\n    document.cookie = 'session1=abc-123; httpOnly';\r\n    document.cookie = 'session2=abc-123';\r\n\r\n    document.cookie\r\n        \"session2=abc-123\"\r\n\r\nIt's just a mild concern about [session fixation](https://www.owasp.org/index.php/Session_fixation); as it could be used by someone malicious to create a `httpOnly` session cookie on the victims computer, where the attacker will then know what the value will be (as they set it)... that's not to say that they couldn't set the cookie without the `httpOnly` flag.",
